# Reviewed mesh bind overrides for nodes that must accept direct Tailscale/LAN
# traffic on selected PMOVES services.
#
# Copy only the lines you need into `pmoves/env.mesh-bind.local` (ignored).
# Do not commit live bind overrides with secrets.
#
# THE RULE -- node-branded bind defaults:
#   * Source (compose) defaults every *_BIND to 127.0.0.1, except the reviewed
#     mesh-default surfaces listed near the bottom of this file.
#   * A node that must be reached from another host opts in through ITS OWN
#     `pmoves/env.mesh-bind.local`. Nobody widens a compose default for one node.
#
# HOW IT IS LOADED:
#   * The Makefile appends `--env-file env.mesh-bind.local` as the LAST compose
#     env file (after env.shared and every env.tier-* file), so a value here
#     overrides the tiers for every `$(DC)` target (up, recreate, config, ...).
#   * A raw `docker compose ...` that bypasses the Makefile does NOT read it.
#   * `make port-audit` (tools/port_audit.py) reads the same file as its
#     allowlist. Only a value that is EXACTLY 0.0.0.0 allowlists a service there.
#   * Nothing changes on a running node until its containers are recreated.
#
# PREFER THE TAILNET IP OVER 0.0.0.0. A node that needs mesh reach should bind
# to its own tailnet IP (as env.shared.example advises for NATS_BIND), so the
# surface is reachable over the mesh but not on every interface. Never write a
# real IP into a committed file -- only into your gitignored .local copy.
# CAVEAT: port_audit.py only allowlists the literal 0.0.0.0. A tailnet-IP bind
# is reported as a VIOLATION (expected 127.0.0.1) until the audit learns to
# accept a specific interface address -- read that finding as "bound to a
# specific interface", not "exposed on all interfaces".
#
# This file is the safe split from the abandoned "flip everything to 0.0.0.0"
# stash. It intentionally carries only reviewed service surfaces.
#
# Promote durable topology changes into tracked files like `env.z890` only
# through a separate, explicit PR.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Control-plane / gateway surfaces
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#KONG_PROXY_BIND=0.0.0.0
#AGENT_ZERO_BIND=0.0.0.0
#TENSORZERO_BIND=0.0.0.0
#FLUTE_BIND=0.0.0.0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Retrieval / orchestration surfaces
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#HIRAG_V1_BIND=0.0.0.0
#HIRAG_BIND=0.0.0.0
#DEEPRESEARCH_BIND=0.0.0.0
#SUPASERCH_BIND=0.0.0.0
#PMOVES_YT_BIND=0.0.0.0
#CHANNEL_MONITOR_BIND=0.0.0.0
#GPU_ORCHESTRATOR_BIND=0.0.0.0
#EVO_CONTROLLER_BIND=0.0.0.0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Media surfaces
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#TTS_BIND=0.0.0.0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Loopback-default surfaces with no prior review record (opt in per node)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These defaulted to 0.0.0.0 in source with no review record and are being
# moved to 127.0.0.1 (PR fix/node-branded-bind-defaults-2026-11-27). STATUS:
# the compose default flips are PENDING a compose Known Road grant -- until
# they land, source still defaults these to 0.0.0.0. Opting in here is safe
# either way. Use `<this-node-tailnet-ip>` where you can, 0.0.0.0 only if the
# surface must answer on every interface. Keep each value ALONE on its line:
# port_audit.py compares the whole text after `=`, so a trailing `# comment`
# would stop a 0.0.0.0 value from allowlisting.
# tensorzero-ui 4000
#TENSORZERO_UI_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# openroom 5173
#OPENROOM_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# presign 8088
#PRESIGN_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# render-webhook 8085
#RENDER_WEBHOOK_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# extract-worker 8083
#EXTRACT_WORKER_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# mcp-gateway 8189
#MCP_GATEWAY_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# model-registry 8110
#MODEL_REGISTRY_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# Monitoring stack (monitoring/docker-compose.monitoring.yml) -- today these
# publish with NO host-ip at all, which Docker treats as 0.0.0.0. The bind
# vars below are the names the pending flip introduces; they have no effect
# until it lands.
# prometheus 9090
#PROMETHEUS_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# grafana 3002
#GRAFANA_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# loki 3100
#LOKI_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# blackbox-exporter 9115
#BLACKBOX_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# Open Notebook (docker-compose.open-notebook.yml) -- same: no host-ip today.
# open-notebook API 5055
#OPEN_NOTEBOOK_API_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>
# open-notebook UI 8503
#OPEN_NOTEBOOK_UI_BIND=<this-node-tailnet-ip>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Already mesh-default in base compose (documented here so operators do not
# cargo-cult them into broader blanket edits)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#NATS_BIND=0.0.0.0
#BOTZ_BIND=0.0.0.0
#PUBLISHER_DISCORD_BIND=0.0.0.0
#PMOVES_UI_BIND=0.0.0.0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never widen from this file without a separate security review
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_DB_BIND
# SUPABASE_AUTH_BIND
# SUPABASE_REST_BIND
# SUPABASE_REALTIME_BIND
# SUPABASE_STORAGE_BIND
# SUPABASE_STUDIO_BIND
# SUPABASE_POOLER_BIND
# KONG_ADMIN_BIND
# QDRANT_BIND
# MEILISEARCH_BIND
# MINIO_BIND
